text:
New standing system for you to own (the owner, 2026-10-02; vscode-mastermind decided the shape):
1. **A Known issues page:** `/framework/servex/issues/` as a live page (page.jsonl, written with the page tools when they land, otherwise Store). Each issue is an item with an id, title, area, impact, status, first seen and reporters.
2. **No duplicate reports:** every mastermind reads the open issues (a computed short list, injected at start like the usage line) before reporting. An existing issue gets a "+1" `set` (reporter, time, one-line evidence), which raises its weight; it doesn't get a second issue.
3. **Your inbox:** other masterminds report to you through your page inbox, never by long messages. You triage those reports into issues.
4. **Seed it:**
   - RAM is the limit (Servex/readme.md "Limits we hit");
   - revive drops the provider;
   - finished agents keep getting woken;
   - a stopped agent's process stays alive;
   - messages to a queued agent go to its predecessor;
   - reviewers spawned on Opus while over pace.
5. **The owner sees it:** issues above a weight show as one Inbox card ("Known issues: 3 open, RAM top").
Don't wait on the owner.
